{{- /*
orders.gohtml is the order list.

The rows come from the cross-module read layer, not from a module's service: the
panel knows no module (ADR 0011). Every field is printed as an ordinary value,
so the template engine's escaping applies to all of them — an order's e-mail is
customer-supplied text and the panel runs inside an administrator's session.

Paging shows "next" only when the read returned one record more than the page
holds. There is no total and no last page: a count over a growing order table is
the expensive half of paging (3.03 ms against 0.47 ms for the page itself, on a
52,000-row fixture) and an operator does not need to be told how many orders
exist in total.
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<h1>{{ .Title }}</h1>

{{ if .Orders }}
<div class="scroll">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Order</th><th>Status</th><th>Customer</th>
      <th class="num">Total</th><th>Placed</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {{ range .Orders }}
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{ $.Path }}/{{ .ID }}">#{{ .DisplayID }}</a></td>
      <td><span class="pill">{{ .Status }}</span></td>
      <td>{{ if .Email }}{{ .Email }}{{ else }}<span class="muted">no address</span>{{ end }}</td>
      {{- /*
      An amount whose currency scale could not be read is shown as minor units
      and SAID to be, rather than being divided by a guessed hundred: that would
      print the wrong figure for every 0-digit and 3-digit currency.
      */ -}}
      <td class="num">
        {{ .Total }} {{ .Currency }}{{ if .Minor }} <span class="muted">(minor)</span>{{ end }}
      </td>
      <td>{{ if not .PlacedAt.IsZero }}{{ .PlacedAt.Format "2006-01-02 15:04" }}{{ end }}</td>
    </tr>
  {{ end }}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{ else }}
<p class="muted">No orders on this page.</p>
{{ end }}

<nav>
  {{ if .HasPrev }}<a href="{{ .Path }}?page={{ .PrevPage }}">Previous</a>{{ end }}
  <span class="muted">Page {{ .Page }}</span>
  {{ if .HasNext }}<a href="{{ .Path }}?page={{ .NextPage }}">Next</a>{{ end }}
</nav>
{{ end }}
